        "bbox_px": [
          289.828125,
          999.0,
          1437.75,
          1374.0
        ],
        "text": "<p block-type=\"Text\">The sensitivity and variability of the Borgwaldt unit will be determined by testing cigarettes of a single blend at five different. weight levels on both the Borgwaldt instrument and the PM compacimeter. This portion of the experiment will be performed three times to ensure the accuracy of the results. Cigarettes will also be tested at two circumference levels and five weight levels to determine the sensitivity of the Borgwaldt unit to circumference variation. In addition, a set of cigarettes will be tested with three different seam orientations to determine the sensitivity of Borgwaldt firmness results to seam position. The data from these experiments will be analyzed to determine the sensitivity and variability of the Borgwaldt instrument so it can be compared with the PM compacimeter.</p>"
